## Two things worth your attention

**The fleet manifest instruction is a live regression risk.** The manifest is still dated 2026-03-08 — five months stale, and missing HUB and pub entirely. CLAUDE.md says "the manifest is the source of truth — the page follows it." Following that literally would regress five model strings (Thor 3.5 27B → 2.5 14B, CBP back to TinyLlama, etc.) and reintroduce a mismatch prior cycles fixed. I declined, third cycle running. Either the manifest gets an owner or Step 0 should be rewritten to "reconcile and report."

**So what:** the terminology mission is done and has been for several cycles. What the audits surface now is one tier up — not "is the term expanded right" but "is the claim *about* the term true, attributed, and hedged the same on every page." All four substantive fixes were that kind; none would have been caught by a drift grep.

The uncomfortable part: this track is now good at making an honest site more precisely honest, and that isn't the binding constraint. The site's two headline claims each have a specified falsification test nobody has run, and the fleet's 31+ daily tracks include zero experiments. I can add clauses indefinitely without moving that. The scramble control needs one machine and a permuted corpus — whether this track should own it is your call, but I'd rather run it than write another caveat.
